%% ============================================================
%% DIAGRAM 04: RECOMMENDATION WORKFLOW
%% ============================================================
%% PURPOSE:
%% Shows how approved preferences become a ranked list of real songs.
%%
%% PLAIN-LANGUAGE EXPLANATION:
%% VYBE loads public songs and private songs owned by the current anonymous session.
%% It removes excluded songs, retrieves textually relevant candidates with local
%% TF-IDF, and measures how well their music features match reviewed preferences.
%% The hybrid score uses 35 percent retrieval relevance and 65 percent feature
%% similarity. If text retrieval finds nothing, feature scoring safely uses the
%% eligible catalog instead.
%%
%% HOW TO READ:
%% Follow the numbered messages from top to bottom. The two branches show behavior
%% with and without positive text-retrieval matches.
%%
%% KEY POINT:
%% Ranking is local, deterministic, catalog-grounded, and reproducible.
%% ============================================================
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Listener
    participant UI
    participant API
    participant Catalog
    participant Retrieval
    participant Scorer as Feature Scorer
    participant Hybrid as Hybrid Ranker
    participant Ground as Evidence Renderer

    Note over Listener,Ground: Inputs are reviewed preferences plus caller-visible catalog records

    Listener->>UI: Apply and correct interpreted preferences
    UI->>API: Query plus reviewed preferences
    API->>Catalog: Load public and caller-private songs
    API->>API: Apply exclusions
    API->>Retrieval: Retrieve up to configured candidate count
    alt Positive retrieval matches
        Retrieval-->>Hybrid: Candidates and text relevance
        Hybrid->>Hybrid: Normalize retrieval scores
        Hybrid->>Scorer: Score reviewed feature similarity
        Scorer-->>Hybrid: Feature scores and reasons
        Hybrid->>Hybrid: 35% retrieval + 65% features
    else No retrieval match
        Retrieval-->>Hybrid: Empty candidate set
        Hybrid->>Scorer: Score full eligible catalog
        Scorer-->>Hybrid: Feature-only scores and reasons
    end
    Hybrid->>Ground: Ranked songs and validated evidence
    Ground-->>UI: Scores, components, reasons, and grounded prose
    Note over Retrieval,Ground: Stable calculations make the same inputs produce the same ranking
